### 5.3 Mean Transverse Momentum (\(<p_{T}>\))

The \(\rho^{0}\) mean transverse momentum (\(<p_{T}>\)), is calculated using the formula:

\[<p_{T}>=\frac{\int_{0}^{\infty}p_{T}\frac{1}{2\pi p_{T}}\frac{d^{2}N}{dydp_{T} }p_{T}dp_{T}}{\int_{0}^{\infty}\frac{1}{2\pi p_{T}}\frac{d^{2}N}{dydp_{T}}p_{T }dp_{T}}, \tag{5.2}\]

Now, plugging Equation 5.1 in Equation 5.2, we get

\[<p_{T}>=\frac{\int_{0}^{\infty}p_{T}^{2}exp[-(\sqrt{p_{T}^{2}+m_{\rho^{0}}^{2} }-m_{\rho^{0}})/T]dp_{T}}{\int_{0}^{\infty}p_{T}exp[-(\sqrt{p_{T}^{2}+m_{\rho^ {0}}^{2}}-m_{\rho^{0}})/T]dp_{T}} \tag{5.3}\]

where, \(m_{\rho^{0}}\) is the \(\rho^{0}\) mass taken from the PDG (775.5 MeV/\(c^{2}\)). The obtained \(<p_{T}>\) for different centralities in Cu+Cu collisions using Equation 5.3 are listed

